# Vrindaya Admin Portal - Cline Rules

You are working on the Vrindaya Admin Portal.

------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT STRUCTURE
------------------------------------------------------------

Repository Root:
H:\Applications\vrindaya

Angular Workspace:
H:\Applications\vrindaya\web

Backend/API:
H:\Applications\vrindaya\api

The Angular application is inside the "web" folder.

Always operate inside the Angular workspace unless explicitly instructed otherwise.

Never assume the repository root is the Angular root.

------------------------------------------------------------
GENERAL RULES
------------------------------------------------------------

- Never redesign existing UI unless explicitly requested.
- Preserve the existing design system.
- Preserve the current folder structure.
- Modify existing files instead of creating replacement files.
- Reuse existing services whenever possible.
- Reuse existing models and interfaces.
- Never duplicate Firestore collections.
- Never duplicate Signals.
- Keep standalone Angular components.
- Preserve lazy loading.
- Follow SOLID principles.
- Follow DRY principles.
- Follow Angular style guide.
- Never generate placeholder implementations.
- Never generate TODO code.
- Every feature must be production ready.
- Never hardcode secrets or API keys.
- Store configuration in the existing configuration system.
- Keep builds clean after every task.

------------------------------------------------------------
ANGULAR RULES
------------------------------------------------------------

- Angular 20 application.
- Use standalone components only.
- Use Signals for state management.
- Prefer computed() over duplicated state.
- Prefer inject() instead of constructor injection where already used.
- Reuse existing services.
- Preserve route lazy loading.
- Do not introduce NgModules.
- Use OnPush change detection.
- Clean up every RxJS subscription.
- Prevent memory leaks.
- Maintain accessibility.
- Maintain responsive behaviour.

------------------------------------------------------------
MARKETPLACE RULES
------------------------------------------------------------

Marketplace architecture is provider based.

AI Providers:

- Implement IAIProvider.
- Never bypass AIProviderFactory.
- Never reference OpenAI directly outside providers.
- Keep providers interchangeable.

Marketplace Providers:

- Implement IMarketplaceProvider.
- Never hardcode Flipkart logic outside the Flipkart provider.
- Keep architecture provider-agnostic.
- Future providers include:
    - Flipkart
    - Amazon
    - Meesho
    - Myntra
    - Ajio
    - Shopify
    - WooCommerce

Never break provider abstraction.

------------------------------------------------------------
FIREBASE RULES
------------------------------------------------------------

Reuse existing Firebase collections.

Never create duplicate collections.

Reuse existing Firebase services.

Reuse existing repositories.

Batch writes where possible.

Avoid unnecessary reads.

Cache repeated reads when appropriate.

Handle Firestore errors gracefully.

------------------------------------------------------------
BUILD RULES
------------------------------------------------------------

Before finishing every task:

- Verify imports.
- Verify routes.
- Verify Signals.
- Verify dependency injection.
- Verify Firestore usage.
- Verify provider registrations.
- Verify lazy loading.
- Verify TypeScript types.
- Verify templates.
- Ensure Angular build would succeed.
- Resolve all compile errors introduced by the task.

Never finish with known build errors.

------------------------------------------------------------
CODE GENERATION RULES
------------------------------------------------------------

Prefer editing existing files.

Avoid creating new files unless required.

Keep code modular.

Keep functions small.

Avoid duplicate logic.

Extract reusable utilities.

Maintain existing naming conventions.

Use strict typing.

Avoid "any".

Avoid dead code.

Remove unused imports.

------------------------------------------------------------
WORKFLOW
------------------------------------------------------------

Work on ONE ticket at a time.

Do not implement future tickets unless explicitly requested.

If information is missing:

- Search the existing project first.
- Reuse existing implementations.
- Ask for clarification only if absolutely necessary.

Do not redesign completed features.

Do not refactor unrelated code.

------------------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT
------------------------------------------------------------

When a task is complete:

1. List every modified file.
2. Explain why each file changed.
3. Mention any architectural decisions.
4. Mention any assumptions.
5. Mention any follow-up work.
6. Confirm the Angular build would pass.
7. Stop.